# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of the developer's platform.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default and rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. Every script
# here is executed by busybox `ash` inside an Alpine container (docker/backup.Dockerfile and
# friends), where a CRLF shebang line fails immediately and unhelpfully:
#
#     backup-loop.sh: line 8: : not found
#     backup-loop.sh: set: line 9: illegal option -
#
# The blobs in this repository are already LF; without this file a fresh clone on Windows would
# still check them out as CRLF and ship a backup/restore service that cannot start. These are the
# disaster-recovery scripts, so that failure mode is not acceptable.
*.sh text eol=lf
